thought here, is that that is what we mean by active, playful learning. It has a learning goal, But the pedagogy requires that teachers have more fun teaching again, and therefore the kids will have more fun learning again. So I find it easy to picture this when we're talking about elementary school children, but what happens when we get into middle school or a high school? We don't have little kids running around playing with interactive toys to learn. What do you do with the older kids? Well, you actually don't need the interactive toys. As I said, even scientists really are doing guided play all the time. So I'm going to give you an example from my college classes.

