Now I grant it, this is two years old, so maybe everything's changed, but I doubt it. And at that time, only two of the apps actually made it to what we would call in the science. Educational. That's astounding. Now you say, but, okay, a lot of kids aren't spending time on apps, are they? Well, by middle school, they're spending 14 hours a day on this stuff. Now, think about that. That's over a 70-hour work week that they're spending in front of a screen.

