and when we are and our kids see us in front of the screen all the time and not looking in their eyes, their message to the child is, I'm not as important as the screen is. And in fact, I want you to know that for this program, I pulled my grandchildren over Thanksgiving. And I said, well, does it disturb you when adults are on phones a lot? This is a six and eight year old, and they said, yeah. and I said, why? I said, well, we don't get any attention. They're just sitting looking at their phone

